{"cells":[{"cell_type":"markdown","metadata":{"id":"bf3fb144"},"source":["# 2 — Promedio ponderado y self-attention\n","\n","Segundo milestone, sobre el **Notebook 1 (bigrama simple)**. Acá construimos el mecanismo central de la atención en tres pasos:\n","\n","1. **El truco matemático**: las cuatro versiones del promedio ponderado del pasado, del for-loop a la self-attention.\n","2. **Modelo v2**: un bigrama que usa ese promedio **uniforme** como memoria del pasado (sin atención).\n","3. **Modelo v3**: el mismo modelo, pero reemplazando el promedio uniforme por **una cabeza de self-attention** (+ posición).\n","\n","Este notebook es autocontenido: la Sección 0 repite el setup del Notebook 1."],"id":"bf3fb144"},{"cell_type":"markdown","metadata":{"id":"c57b7ee8"},"source":["## Sección 0 — Setup\n","\n","Igual que en el Notebook 1: descargamos el dataset, armamos el vocabulario de caracteres, `encode`/`decode`, el split train/val y el `get_batch`. Se agregan tres cosas:\n","\n","- `device`: usa GPU si el runtime de Colab tiene una (Runtime → Change runtime type → GPU); si no, CPU.\n","- `estimate_loss(model)`: reporta el loss de train y val promediando varios batches, con `@torch.no_grad()`.\n","- `train(model)`: el loop de entrenamiento, para reutilizarlo con v2 y v3."],"id":"c57b7ee8"},{"cell_type":"code","metadata":{"colab":{"base_uri":"https://localhost:8080/"},"id":"faab66df","executionInfo":{"status":"ok","timestamp":1786454098821,"user_tz":180,"elapsed":515,"user":{"displayName":"Francisco Traversaro","userId":"11717466918051452843"}},"outputId":"297b47db-7876-49fd-f519-751bc0de2043"},"source":["# descargamos el tiny shakespeare dataset\n","!wget https://raw.githubusercontent.com/karpathy/char-rnn/master/data/tinyshakespeare/input.txt"],"id":"faab66df","execution_count":1,"outputs":[{"output_type":"stream","name":"stdout","text":["--2026-08-11 13:14:58--  https://raw.githubusercontent.com/karpathy/char-rnn/master/data/tinyshakespeare/input.txt\n","Resolving raw.githubusercontent.com (raw.githubusercontent.com)... 185.199.108.133, 185.199.109.133, 185.199.110.133, ...\n","Connecting to raw.githubusercontent.com (raw.githubusercontent.com)|185.199.108.133|:443... connected.\n","HTTP request sent, awaiting response... 200 OK\n","Length: 1115394 (1.1M) [text/plain]\n","Saving to: ‘input.txt’\n","\n","input.txt           100%[===================>]   1.06M  --.-KB/s    in 0.006s  \n","\n","2026-08-11 13:14:58 (190 MB/s) - ‘input.txt’ saved [1115394/1115394]\n","\n"]}]},{"cell_type":"code","metadata":{"colab":{"base_uri":"https://localhost:8080/"},"id":"f5fd569c","executionInfo":{"status":"ok","timestamp":1786454106960,"user_tz":180,"elapsed":8133,"user":{"displayName":"Francisco Traversaro","userId":"11717466918051452843"}},"outputId":"bffaad93-b865-44c5-f8d2-29534ff863c7"},"source":["import torch\n","import torch.nn as nn\n","from torch.nn import functional as F\n","\n","torch.manual_seed(1337)\n","device = 'cuda' if torch.cuda.is_available() else 'cpu'\n","print('device:', device)"],"id":"f5fd569c","execution_count":2,"outputs":[{"output_type":"stream","name":"stdout","text":["device: cuda\n"]}]},{"cell_type":"code","metadata":{"colab":{"base_uri":"https://localhost:8080/"},"id":"ffa3bcdc","executionInfo":{"status":"ok","timestamp":1786454107009,"user_tz":180,"elapsed":41,"user":{"displayName":"Francisco Traversaro","userId":"11717466918051452843"}},"outputId":"139f52ed-2a60-4eaa-f570-1b55d09b00fb"},"source":["# leemos el texto y armamos el vocabulario de caracteres\n","with open('input.txt', 'r', encoding='utf-8') as f:\n","    text = f.read()\n","\n","chars = sorted(list(set(text)))\n","vocab_size = len(chars)\n","print('vocab_size =', vocab_size)\n","print(''.join(chars))"],"id":"ffa3bcdc","execution_count":3,"outputs":[{"output_type":"stream","name":"stdout","text":["vocab_size = 65\n","\n"," !$&',-.3:;?ABCDEFGHIJKLMNOPQRSTUVWXYZabcdefghijklmnopqrstuvwxyz\n"]}]},{"cell_type":"code","metadata":{"id":"a75d8aef","executionInfo":{"status":"ok","timestamp":1786454107044,"user_tz":180,"elapsed":19,"user":{"displayName":"Francisco Traversaro","userId":"11717466918051452843"}}},"source":["# mapeo caracteres <-> enteros\n","stoi = { ch:i for i,ch in enumerate(chars) }\n","itos = { i:ch for i,ch in enumerate(chars) }\n","encode = lambda s: [stoi[c] for c in s]          # string -> lista de enteros\n","decode = lambda l: ''.join([itos[i] for i in l]) # lista de enteros -> string"],"id":"a75d8aef","execution_count":4,"outputs":[]},{"cell_type":"code","metadata":{"id":"53f9b1c6","executionInfo":{"status":"ok","timestamp":1786454107395,"user_tz":180,"elapsed":346,"user":{"displayName":"Francisco Traversaro","userId":"11717466918051452843"}}},"source":["# codificamos todo el dataset y hacemos el split train/val\n","data = torch.tensor(encode(text), dtype=torch.long)\n","n = int(0.9*len(data))\n","train_data = data[:n]\n","val_data   = data[n:]"],"id":"53f9b1c6","execution_count":5,"outputs":[]},{"cell_type":"code","metadata":{"id":"8ea129c6","executionInfo":{"status":"ok","timestamp":1786454107415,"user_tz":180,"elapsed":15,"user":{"displayName":"Francisco Traversaro","userId":"11717466918051452843"}}},"source":["# hiperparámetros\n","block_size    = 8      # longitud máxima de contexto\n","batch_size    = 32     # secuencias en paralelo\n","n_embd        = 32     # dimensión de embedding (ahora un embedding de verdad, no los logits)\n","learning_rate = 1e-3\n","max_iters     = 10000\n","eval_interval = 500\n","eval_iters    = 200\n","\n","def get_batch(split):\n","    data = train_data if split == 'train' else val_data\n","    ix = torch.randint(len(data) - block_size, (batch_size,))\n","    x = torch.stack([data[i:i+block_size]     for i in ix])\n","    y = torch.stack([data[i+1:i+block_size+1] for i in ix])\n","    x, y = x.to(device), y.to(device)\n","    return x, y\n","\n","@torch.no_grad()\n","def estimate_loss(model):\n","    out = {}\n","    model.eval()\n","    for split in ['train', 'val']:\n","        losses = torch.zeros(eval_iters)\n","        for k in range(eval_iters):\n","            X, Y = get_batch(split)\n","            _, loss = model(X, Y)\n","            losses[k] = loss.item()\n","        out[split] = losses.mean().item()\n","    model.train()\n","    return out\n","\n","def train(model, max_iters=max_iters):\n","    optimizer = torch.optim.AdamW(model.parameters(), lr=learning_rate)\n","    for it in range(max_iters):\n","        if it % eval_interval == 0 or it == max_iters - 1:\n","            losses = estimate_loss(model)\n","            print(f\"step {it:4d}: train loss {losses['train']:.4f}, val loss {losses['val']:.4f}\")\n","        xb, yb = get_batch('train')\n","        _, loss = model(xb, yb)\n","        optimizer.zero_grad(set_to_none=True)\n","        loss.backward()\n","        optimizer.step()\n","    return model"],"id":"8ea129c6","execution_count":6,"outputs":[]},{"cell_type":"markdown","metadata":{"id":"a25450c8"},"source":["## Sección 1 — El truco matemático: las 4 versiones del promedio ponderado\n","\n","Queremos que cada token se enriquezca con información del pasado. El primer intento, el más simple, es que la representación de cada token sea el **promedio** de todos los tokens hasta él (incluido él mismo) — un \"bag of words\" del pasado. Ojo con lo causal: sólo promediamos hacia atrás, nunca el futuro.\n","\n","Lo construimos de cuatro formas **equivalentes**, cada vez más elegante. Las tres primeras dan exactamente el mismo `xbow` (lo verificamos con `torch.allclose`); la cuarta reemplaza el promedio uniforme por pesos que dependen del contenido — la atención."],"id":"a25450c8"},{"cell_type":"code","metadata":{"colab":{"base_uri":"https://localhost:8080/"},"id":"a7db58da","executionInfo":{"status":"ok","timestamp":1786454107742,"user_tz":180,"elapsed":12,"user":{"displayName":"Francisco Traversaro","userId":"11717466918051452843"}},"outputId":"822d2617-97d4-4b58-ca9d-048fc64abff4"},"source":["# ejemplo de juguete: B secuencias, T posiciones, C canales\n","torch.manual_seed(1337)\n","B, T, C = 4, 8, 2\n","x = torch.randn(B, T, C)\n","x.shape"],"id":"a7db58da","execution_count":7,"outputs":[{"output_type":"execute_result","data":{"text/plain":["torch.Size([4, 8, 2])"]},"metadata":{},"execution_count":7}]},{"cell_type":"markdown","metadata":{"id":"95efb9b5"},"source":["### Versión 1 — el for-loop\n","\n","La forma directa: para cada posición `t`, promediar las representaciones desde el inicio hasta `t`. Correcto, pero lento (dos loops en Python)."],"id":"95efb9b5"},{"cell_type":"code","metadata":{"colab":{"base_uri":"https://localhost:8080/"},"id":"1d91e529","executionInfo":{"status":"ok","timestamp":1786454107765,"user_tz":180,"elapsed":15,"user":{"displayName":"Francisco Traversaro","userId":"11717466918051452843"}},"outputId":"5f7c9f2d-6652-457d-8794-26345495ca5e"},"source":["# queremos xbow[b,t] = promedio de x[b,i] para i <= t\n","xbow = torch.zeros((B, T, C))\n","for b in range(B):\n","    for t in range(T):\n","        xprev = x[b, :t+1]          # (t+1, C) -- los tokens hasta t (incluido)\n","        xbow[b, t] = torch.mean(xprev, 0)\n","xbow[0]"],"id":"1d91e529","execution_count":8,"outputs":[{"output_type":"execute_result","data":{"text/plain":["tensor([[ 0.1808, -0.0700],\n","        [-0.0894, -0.4926],\n","        [ 0.1490, -0.3199],\n","        [ 0.3504, -0.2238],\n","        [ 0.3525,  0.0545],\n","        [ 0.0688, -0.0396],\n","        [ 0.0927, -0.0682],\n","        [-0.0341,  0.1332]])"]},"metadata":{},"execution_count":8}]},{"cell_type":"markdown","metadata":{"id":"1bd8304e"},"source":["### La idea clave: la agregación ponderada es un producto de matrices\n","\n","Una matriz triangular inferior normalizada, multiplicada por los datos, produce el promedio acumulado de las filas — todas las posiciones de una sola vez. Ese es el truco que reaparece hasta el final."],"id":"1bd8304e"},{"cell_type":"code","metadata":{"colab":{"base_uri":"https://localhost:8080/"},"id":"b1cfebcf","executionInfo":{"status":"ok","timestamp":1786454107780,"user_tz":180,"elapsed":12,"user":{"displayName":"Francisco Traversaro","userId":"11717466918051452843"}},"outputId":"c39ce214-9e95-417f-fa8e-95c2077f09c2"},"source":["# por qué un matmul hace la agregación\n","torch.manual_seed(42)\n","a = torch.tril(torch.ones(3, 3))\n","a = a / torch.sum(a, 1, keepdim=True)\n","b = torch.randint(0, 10, (3, 2)).float()\n","c = a @ b\n","print('a =');            print(a)\n","print('b =');            print(b)\n","print('c = a @ b =');    print(c)   # cada fila de c = promedio acumulado de las filas de b"],"id":"b1cfebcf","execution_count":9,"outputs":[{"output_type":"stream","name":"stdout","text":["a =\n","tensor([[1.0000, 0.0000, 0.0000],\n","        [0.5000, 0.5000, 0.0000],\n","        [0.3333, 0.3333, 0.3333]])\n","b =\n","tensor([[2., 7.],\n","        [6., 4.],\n","        [6., 5.]])\n","c = a @ b =\n","tensor([[2.0000, 7.0000],\n","        [4.0000, 5.5000],\n","        [4.6667, 5.3333]])\n"]}]},{"cell_type":"markdown","metadata":{"id":"803373e4"},"source":["### Versión 2 — matmul\n","\n","El promedio del pasado sale de una matriz triangular inferior de unos, normalizada para que cada fila sume 1. `wei @ x` da el mismo `xbow` que el for-loop, en un solo matmul."],"id":"803373e4"},{"cell_type":"code","metadata":{"colab":{"base_uri":"https://localhost:8080/"},"id":"92a0c05d","executionInfo":{"status":"ok","timestamp":1786454107797,"user_tz":180,"elapsed":13,"user":{"displayName":"Francisco Traversaro","userId":"11717466918051452843"}},"outputId":"28045111-15b6-4836-9d4c-4d1b2c8e3f12"},"source":["wei = torch.tril(torch.ones(T, T))\n","wei = wei / wei.sum(1, keepdim=True)\n","xbow2 = wei @ x                      # (T,T) @ (B,T,C) -> (B,T,C)\n","print(wei)\n","print('igual al for-loop?', torch.allclose(xbow, xbow2, rtol = 0.001))"],"id":"92a0c05d","execution_count":10,"outputs":[{"output_type":"stream","name":"stdout","text":["tensor([[1.0000, 0.0000, 0.0000, 0.0000, 0.0000, 0.0000, 0.0000, 0.0000],\n","        [0.5000, 0.5000, 0.0000, 0.0000, 0.0000, 0.0000, 0.0000, 0.0000],\n","        [0.3333, 0.3333, 0.3333, 0.0000, 0.0000, 0.0000, 0.0000, 0.0000],\n","        [0.2500, 0.2500, 0.2500, 0.2500, 0.0000, 0.0000, 0.0000, 0.0000],\n","        [0.2000, 0.2000, 0.2000, 0.2000, 0.2000, 0.0000, 0.0000, 0.0000],\n","        [0.1667, 0.1667, 0.1667, 0.1667, 0.1667, 0.1667, 0.0000, 0.0000],\n","        [0.1429, 0.1429, 0.1429, 0.1429, 0.1429, 0.1429, 0.1429, 0.0000],\n","        [0.1250, 0.1250, 0.1250, 0.1250, 0.1250, 0.1250, 0.1250, 0.1250]])\n","igual al for-loop? True\n"]}]},{"cell_type":"markdown","metadata":{"id":"283597a2"},"source":["### Versión 3 — softmax\n","\n","La que abre la puerta a la atención. Partimos de una matriz de afinidades en cero, enmascaramos el futuro con `-inf`, y aplicamos softmax por fila. `exp(-inf)=0` mata el futuro, y softmax de valores iguales da uniforme: recuperamos los mismos pesos."],"id":"283597a2"},{"cell_type":"code","metadata":{"colab":{"base_uri":"https://localhost:8080/"},"id":"1d583446","executionInfo":{"status":"ok","timestamp":1786454107816,"user_tz":180,"elapsed":13,"user":{"displayName":"Francisco Traversaro","userId":"11717466918051452843"}},"outputId":"32b4c176-0e2b-4bed-8b86-353d97db897b"},"source":["tril = torch.tril(torch.ones(T, T))\n","wei = torch.zeros((T, T))\n","wei = wei.masked_fill(tril == 0, float('-inf'))  # el futuro a -inf\n","print(wei)\n","wei = F.softmax(wei, dim=-1)                       # softmax por fila -> uniforme causal\n","xbow3 = wei @ x\n","print(wei)\n","print('igual al for-loop?', torch.allclose(xbow, xbow3, rtol = 0.001))"],"id":"1d583446","execution_count":11,"outputs":[{"output_type":"stream","name":"stdout","text":["tensor([[0., -inf, -inf, -inf, -inf, -inf, -inf, -inf],\n","        [0., 0., -inf, -inf, -inf, -inf, -inf, -inf],\n","        [0., 0., 0., -inf, -inf, -inf, -inf, -inf],\n","        [0., 0., 0., 0., -inf, -inf, -inf, -inf],\n","        [0., 0., 0., 0., 0., -inf, -inf, -inf],\n","        [0., 0., 0., 0., 0., 0., -inf, -inf],\n","        [0., 0., 0., 0., 0., 0., 0., -inf],\n","        [0., 0., 0., 0., 0., 0., 0., 0.]])\n","tensor([[1.0000, 0.0000, 0.0000, 0.0000, 0.0000, 0.0000, 0.0000, 0.0000],\n","        [0.5000, 0.5000, 0.0000, 0.0000, 0.0000, 0.0000, 0.0000, 0.0000],\n","        [0.3333, 0.3333, 0.3333, 0.0000, 0.0000, 0.0000, 0.0000, 0.0000],\n","        [0.2500, 0.2500, 0.2500, 0.2500, 0.0000, 0.0000, 0.0000, 0.0000],\n","        [0.2000, 0.2000, 0.2000, 0.2000, 0.2000, 0.0000, 0.0000, 0.0000],\n","        [0.1667, 0.1667, 0.1667, 0.1667, 0.1667, 0.1667, 0.0000, 0.0000],\n","        [0.1429, 0.1429, 0.1429, 0.1429, 0.1429, 0.1429, 0.1429, 0.0000],\n","        [0.1250, 0.1250, 0.1250, 0.1250, 0.1250, 0.1250, 0.1250, 0.1250]])\n","igual al for-loop? True\n"]}]},{"cell_type":"markdown","metadata":{"id":"cf3c5d10"},"source":["### Versión 4 — self-attention\n","\n","Ahora los pesos dejan de ser uniformes. Cada token proyecta una *query* y una *key*; la afinidad `q·k` decide cuánto atiende cada token a cada token del pasado. El resto del andamiaje —máscara causal, softmax— es idéntico. Y se agrega un *value*: la salida es el promedio ponderado de los **values**, no de `x`."],"id":"cf3c5d10"},{"cell_type":"code","metadata":{"colab":{"base_uri":"https://localhost:8080/"},"id":"a38f6ef2","executionInfo":{"status":"ok","timestamp":1786454107837,"user_tz":180,"elapsed":15,"user":{"displayName":"Francisco Traversaro","userId":"11717466918051452843"}},"outputId":"121cd38f-b36e-4517-b253-a2f4bcd9ac39"},"source":["torch.manual_seed(1337)\n","B, T, C = 4, 8, 32     # ahora C más grande\n","x = torch.randn(B, T, C)\n","\n","head_size = 16\n","key   = nn.Linear(C, head_size, bias=False)\n","query = nn.Linear(C, head_size, bias=False)\n","value = nn.Linear(C, head_size, bias=False)\n","k = key(x)     # (B,T,head_size)\n","q = query(x)   # (B,T,head_size)\n","wei = q @ k.transpose(-2, -1)                       # (B,T,T) -- afinidades q·k\n","\n","tril = torch.tril(torch.ones(T, T))\n","wei = wei.masked_fill(tril == 0, float('-inf'))     # máscara causal\n","wei = F.softmax(wei, dim=-1)\n","\n","v = value(x)   # (B,T,head_size)\n","out = wei @ v  # (B,T,head_size)\n","\n","print(wei[0])  # el mapa de atención de la 1a secuencia: ya NO es uniforme\n","out.shape"],"id":"a38f6ef2","execution_count":12,"outputs":[{"output_type":"stream","name":"stdout","text":["tensor([[1.0000, 0.0000, 0.0000, 0.0000, 0.0000, 0.0000, 0.0000, 0.0000],\n","        [0.1574, 0.8426, 0.0000, 0.0000, 0.0000, 0.0000, 0.0000, 0.0000],\n","        [0.2088, 0.1646, 0.6266, 0.0000, 0.0000, 0.0000, 0.0000, 0.0000],\n","        [0.5792, 0.1187, 0.1889, 0.1131, 0.0000, 0.0000, 0.0000, 0.0000],\n","        [0.0294, 0.1052, 0.0469, 0.0276, 0.7909, 0.0000, 0.0000, 0.0000],\n","        [0.0176, 0.2689, 0.0215, 0.0089, 0.6812, 0.0019, 0.0000, 0.0000],\n","        [0.1691, 0.4066, 0.0438, 0.0416, 0.1048, 0.2012, 0.0329, 0.0000],\n","        [0.0210, 0.0843, 0.0555, 0.2297, 0.0573, 0.0709, 0.2423, 0.2391]],\n","       grad_fn=<SelectBackward0>)\n"]},{"output_type":"execute_result","data":{"text/plain":["torch.Size([4, 8, 16])"]},"metadata":{},"execution_count":12}]},{"cell_type":"markdown","metadata":{"id":"70b25397"},"source":["### (Opcional) El escalado 1/√(head_size)\n","\n","Sin escalar, la varianza de `q·k` crece con `head_size` y el softmax se satura (queda casi one-hot), apagando el gradiente. Dividir por `√(head_size)` mantiene la varianza en ~1."],"id":"70b25397"},{"cell_type":"code","metadata":{"colab":{"base_uri":"https://localhost:8080/"},"id":"c962d460","executionInfo":{"status":"ok","timestamp":1786454107867,"user_tz":180,"elapsed":20,"user":{"displayName":"Francisco Traversaro","userId":"11717466918051452843"}},"outputId":"142cbd23-f102-446a-d43b-d502e156ff2a"},"source":["torch.manual_seed(1337)\n","k = torch.randn(B, T, head_size)\n","q = torch.randn(B, T, head_size)\n","wei_sin = q @ k.transpose(-2, -1)\n","wei_con = q @ k.transpose(-2, -1) * head_size**-0.5\n","print('var sin escalar:', wei_sin.var().item())\n","print('var escalado   :', wei_con.var().item())   # ~1\n","\n","# un softmax con valores grandes se vuelve \"picudo\" (converge a one-hot):\n","print(torch.softmax(torch.tensor([0.1, -0.2, 0.3, -0.2, 0.5]),   dim=-1))\n","print(torch.softmax(torch.tensor([0.1, -0.2, 0.3, -0.2, 0.5])*8, dim=-1))"],"id":"c962d460","execution_count":13,"outputs":[{"output_type":"stream","name":"stdout","text":["var sin escalar: 18.44363021850586\n","var escalado   : 1.1527268886566162\n","tensor([0.1925, 0.1426, 0.2351, 0.1426, 0.2872])\n","tensor([0.0326, 0.0030, 0.1615, 0.0030, 0.8000])\n"]}]},{"cell_type":"markdown","metadata":{"id":"da93b2dd"},"source":["## Sección 2 — Modelo v2: el promedio uniforme como memoria\n","\n","Ahora convertimos el truco en un modelo entrenable. Dos cambios respecto del bigrama simple del Notebook 1:\n","\n","- La tabla pasa de `nn.Embedding(vocab_size, vocab_size)` a **`nn.Embedding(vocab_size, n_embd)`**: ya no escupe los logits directamente, sino un vector aprendido de dimensión `n_embd` (acá, 32). Por eso ahora **`C = n_embd`**, no `vocab_size` — exactamente la transición que anticipamos al final del Notebook 1.\n","- Como la representación ya no es el logit, hace falta una capa lineal final, **`lm_head = nn.Linear(n_embd, vocab_size)`**, que proyecta de `n_embd` de vuelta al tamaño del vocabulario para obtener los logits.\n","\n","En el medio, la \"memoria\": el **promedio uniforme causal** del pasado (la versión 3 del truco), con pesos fijos. Todavía **sin positional embedding** — es un bag-of-words puro. Veamos si esta memoria uniforme, por sí sola, ayuda."],"id":"da93b2dd"},{"cell_type":"code","metadata":{"id":"d641aa19","executionInfo":{"status":"ok","timestamp":1786454107869,"user_tz":180,"elapsed":7,"user":{"displayName":"Francisco Traversaro","userId":"11717466918051452843"}}},"source":["class BigramLanguageModelV2(nn.Module):\n","    \"\"\" v2: cada token se contextualiza con un PROMEDIO UNIFORME causal del pasado (memoria, sin atención, sin posición) \"\"\"\n","\n","    def __init__(self):\n","        super().__init__()\n","        self.token_embedding_table = nn.Embedding(vocab_size, n_embd)\n","        self.lm_head = nn.Linear(n_embd, vocab_size)\n","        self.register_buffer('tril', torch.tril(torch.ones(block_size, block_size)))\n","\n","    def forward(self, idx, targets=None):\n","        B, T = idx.shape\n","        tok_emb = self.token_embedding_table(idx)     # (B,T,n_embd)\n","        x = tok_emb                                    # (B,T,n_embd) -- sin posición todavía\n","        # promedio uniforme causal del pasado (versión 3 del truco: pesos fijos y uniformes)\n","        wei = self.tril[:T, :T]\n","        wei = wei / wei.sum(1, keepdim=True)           # cada fila suma 1 -> 1/(t+1)\n","        x = wei @ x                                     # (T,T) @ (B,T,n_embd) -> (B,T,n_embd)\n","        logits = self.lm_head(x)                        # (B,T,vocab_size)\n","\n","        loss = None\n","        if targets is not None:\n","            B, T, C = logits.shape\n","            logits  = logits.view(B*T, C)\n","            targets = targets.view(B*T)\n","            loss = F.cross_entropy(logits, targets)\n","        return logits, loss\n","\n","    def generate(self, idx, max_new_tokens):\n","        for _ in range(max_new_tokens):\n","            idx_cond = idx[:, -block_size:]             # recorte a block_size (por consistencia con v3)\n","            logits, _ = self(idx_cond)\n","            logits = logits[:, -1, :]                   # (B,C) -- último paso temporal\n","            probs = F.softmax(logits, dim=-1)\n","            idx_next = torch.multinomial(probs, num_samples=1)\n","            idx = torch.cat((idx, idx_next), dim=1)\n","        return idx"],"id":"d641aa19","execution_count":14,"outputs":[]},{"cell_type":"code","metadata":{"colab":{"base_uri":"https://localhost:8080/"},"id":"c8a388c9","executionInfo":{"status":"ok","timestamp":1786454146788,"user_tz":180,"elapsed":38916,"user":{"displayName":"Francisco Traversaro","userId":"11717466918051452843"}},"outputId":"d5cd382f-db1a-4663-804e-44ead9cf33cb"},"source":["torch.manual_seed(1337)\n","model_v2 = BigramLanguageModelV2().to(device)\n","print(sum(p.numel() for p in model_v2.parameters())/1e3, 'K parámetros')\n","train(model_v2)"],"id":"c8a388c9","execution_count":15,"outputs":[{"output_type":"stream","name":"stdout","text":["4.225 K parámetros\n","step    0: train loss 4.2777, val loss 4.2702\n","step  500: train loss 3.0283, val loss 3.0391\n","step 1000: train loss 2.9175, val loss 2.9278\n","step 1500: train loss 2.8883, val loss 2.8803\n","step 2000: train loss 2.8592, val loss 2.8635\n","step 2500: train loss 2.8569, val loss 2.8503\n","step 3000: train loss 2.8417, val loss 2.8474\n","step 3500: train loss 2.8411, val loss 2.8357\n","step 4000: train loss 2.8413, val loss 2.8198\n","step 4500: train loss 2.8277, val loss 2.8292\n","step 5000: train loss 2.8182, val loss 2.8391\n","step 5500: train loss 2.8189, val loss 2.8407\n","step 6000: train loss 2.8365, val loss 2.8372\n","step 6500: train loss 2.8239, val loss 2.8152\n","step 7000: train loss 2.8216, val loss 2.8282\n","step 7500: train loss 2.8084, val loss 2.8327\n","step 8000: train loss 2.8124, val loss 2.8156\n","step 8500: train loss 2.8062, val loss 2.8224\n","step 9000: train loss 2.8107, val loss 2.8146\n","step 9500: train loss 2.8066, val loss 2.8207\n","step 9999: train loss 2.8111, val loss 2.8093\n"]},{"output_type":"execute_result","data":{"text/plain":["BigramLanguageModelV2(\n","  (token_embedding_table): Embedding(65, 32)\n","  (lm_head): Linear(in_features=32, out_features=65, bias=True)\n",")"]},"metadata":{},"execution_count":15}]},{"cell_type":"code","metadata":{"colab":{"base_uri":"https://localhost:8080/"},"id":"54434ffd","executionInfo":{"status":"ok","timestamp":1786